  <content>
  <section><para>In this lesson, you will find and interpret the <emphasis>correlation coefficient</emphasis> and use it to understand the strength of a linear relationship.</para>
<para>When you finish this lesson, you will be able to:</para>
<list>
  <item>Describe the “goodness of fit” of a linear model using the correlation coefficient.</item>
  <item>Match the correlation coefficient with a scatter plot and linear model.</item>
</list>
<para>Here are the <emphasis>activities</emphasis> that will help you reach those goals:</para>
<list>
  <item>3.4.0: Lesson Overview</item>
  <item>3.4.1: Compare Scatter Plots with Linear and Nonlinear Trends</item>
  <item>3.4.2: Scatter Plot Differences and Connections to Correlation Coefficient
